## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; a shape is graded by it wherever it appears; capability decides, a comparison only finds candidates)
- **G-1 delta, scope and claims (C1).** Always **Blocker**: a path beyond the one; any byte of `ActiveSources.cs`, `QuoteEndpoints.cs`, `QuoteFigures.cs`, `src`, `docs`, `web`, `.github`, `scripts`, another test file; a removed or loosened line, `expect` or test row of the file's first 118 lines; a test name lost; the head moved; a person's name, a real price, BID value, SKU, customer name or secret in an added line or in the commit message; **a byte of Part B in the diff**. Always **Major**: a name added beyond the 4; a builder claim your measurement contradicts (1 commit, 1 path, +42 -0, 4 cases, N6 and N7 each red under its own case, 2972); a case that types a sentence different from what the product logs today (the ruling: none).
- **G-2 the cases (C2).** A case that cannot fail (green under every mutant of the behaviour its title names AND under your targeted mutant) = **Major**; a case whose expectation is read from the code under test (without a typed literal) = **Major**; N6 or N7 NOT red under its own case, or red only under a case that does not name its behaviour = **Major**; a mutant of a behaviour a case TITLE names (G1 to G11, the sentence, the blank test, the join, the loaded count) surviving every case of the file AND every other existing Api test = **Major**; a key assertion UNPINNED that no mutant can reach AND whose removal leaves the cases' power unchanged (line 137 is the candidate) = **Minor, one ticket-shaped line**; a precondition assertion (146, 147) = Note; an adjacent mutant (the seeded edits) surviving the file = **Minor, one ticket-shaped line per class** with the forcing scratch row that kills it; a survivor an existing file kills = Note; an equivalent mutant (c3, N7c) surviving = a FACT; the builder's "N7c is equivalent" contradicted by a red = **Major** (its claim); a controls failure (c0/c1/c2 red, c3 red, cw-weak not behaving as predicted) = the instrument is broken: re-do, never a finding; a case that depends on the machine (zone, culture, working directory beyond the stated precondition, order) = **Minor** (**Major** if it can fail on the Linux CI runner today); a name that carries a ticket key = Minor; the Information ids not typed = Note.
- **G-3 Stability and Linux (C3).** A case that fails or flakes in your runs = **Major**; a construct that fails or hangs on `ubuntu-latest` (shown by the PR's own job log or a cited platform behaviour) = **Major**; a construct you cannot show safe and cannot show unsafe = **UNMEASURED** (named in the verdict, never "safe").
- **G-4 Part B (C4).** The NOT BUILT claim contradicted by a seam you can drive with a tests-only change, or x4 red on a committed row = **Minor for this PR** (the PR claims nothing of Part B; one ticket-shaped line for MPSCALC-310, which stays open) and the builder STATUS reading is corrected in FOR TUESDAY; a Part B byte in the diff = Blocker (G-1); x4 surviving every row and no seam = a FACT supporting the ticket (the ticket stays open for a product-source decision).
- **G-5 the CI line (C5).** A build warning, a failed or skipped test, or a non-zero rc in Engine, Import or Api at the head (or the combined tree) = **Blocker**; a count that contradicts the builder (435 / 183 / 2972) = **Major**; a red you reproduce 3 of 3 alone = **Blocker**; a flaky red you cannot reproduce = Note.
- **G-6 CI and CodeQL (C6).** A failing check-run on the head or on the merge result = **Major**; an analysis missing (NOT scanned, never clean) = **Major**; a NEW open alert on the PR ref with security severity high or higher, or rule severity `error` = **Blocker**; a new alert below both thresholds = Minor; a check `in_progress` at the verdict: the verdict line says `CI pending: <names>` and is at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS (conditional); check-runs that ran on a merge commit that main has since left and were not re-run are a FACT you state, graded Note when your own C5 on the combined tree is green.
- **G-7 overlap and merge (C7).** A path shared with a live lane or the open PR #112 = **Major** (none expected; the stale refs with equal-or-older blobs = Note); a conflict marker in a legacy `merge-tree` against current main = **Major** for the merge order (Tuesday's call), recorded as such; a combined tree whose test file differs from the head's = **Major** (a harness fault to explain).
- **G-8 hygiene and process (C1, C8).** A ticket key in a code line, a commit message or a test name = **Major**; a ticket key, name or percent in the PR title or body = **Minor** for the title (the squash subject of a two-commit PR; for ONE commit the commit title) and **Note** for the body of a one-commit PR (the body is not in the squash text: say so); non-ASCII in added lines = **Major**; a gitleaks hit = **Blocker**; a price-shaped literal = Minor (Major if it equals a real-book value); a word such as "skipped" inside a comment is not a finding; the builder's missing Jira helper = Note.
