## LOAD (binding; the MPS heavy-slot convention, RELAYED from the B668 and B675 kits)
8 cores; load1 read 4 to 17 across the evening and 8.5 at drafting. Heavy = `dotnet restore`, `dotnet build`, `dotnet test` (including `--list-tests` and every mutant build and run), the full CI line, the whole Api project under the strip mutant, and every scratch-merge build. A git command, a `gh` GET or a Jira GET is light: no slot, one at a time, load1 printed beside it. **Start a heavy run only while `uptime` load1 is below 7** at two reads 4 s apart (not independent: the figure refreshes about every 5 s; say so), recorded beside the result; at 7 or over poll every 20 s, log each wait, and do the light work meanwhile (C1 reading and programs, C2 predictions and the assertion-pin reading, the clone, C6 polling, the Jira GETs). **Then take ONE slot atomically:** `mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-1' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-2' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-3'`, write `B692 <start time> <label>` into its `holder`; read every other holder first (drafter: `heavy-slot-1` holds a B686 holder file; a holder that looks stale is reported, never removed or moved; a slot directory with no holder file is reported, never taken over). All taken: wait 3 minutes and retry. At most ONE slot, one heavy job at a time; **re-read load1 at the start of EACH job inside a held slot**; for a run longer than a few minutes also hold a seat-local lock directory `.tools/b692/heavy.lock` (pid inside, released by a MOVE) so your own waiters never start two jobs; at the run's end release ONLY your own slot, by a MOVE into `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-25_B692_<slot>_<label>/`, never `rm` (if the move is refused, say so and do not work around it). The shared `.tools/.git-lock` wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY (your clone's one `fetch`, `worktree add`), never a build or a test. **A MOVING heartbeat** (a counter plus `date`) goes to `.tools/b692/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; a figure that does not move for 3 beats means the waiter is stuck: say so and what you did. **A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` or `ps ... | grep` on a pattern that appears in its own command line: wait on a recorded PID with `kill -0`, on `wait $!`, or on a done-marker file the job writes last.** Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). Never leave a background job running. NO artificial load, ever. The mutant matrix is one `dotnet build` of the Api test project plus one class run per mutant (medium): batch them inside one slot only while load1 stays below 7 (re-read before each), and release the slot between the whole-solution runs and the matrix so the live builder seat can take one. **NuGet homes are SEAT-LOCAL** (set before the first restore, proven).

## HOLDS
- Datasec / MPS Commercial Calculator only; if any output shows another client's material or another repository's PR, stop reading it and disclose its shape without quoting. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra tenant, Graph, docker, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production site or any app host** (the Api tests host in process; the only listener you may start is on `127.0.0.1` inside 9710-9719, and none is needed). Network: the one explicit-refspec `git fetch` of Step 1 into YOUR clone, `gh api -X GET` under `GH_CONFIG_DIR='<project>/4_Credentials/.gh-config'`, Jira GET as C8 allows (credentials by NAME, in-process, never printed), the NuGet restore into your own seat-local cache. `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh api -X POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE` are forbidden. Never dismiss an alert. No decision-queue tool in any form (not even `list`), no scoreboard, no Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. **No web, node, npm or Playwright run** (no web path in this PR).
- **Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only** (`--no-optional-locks`: `ls-remote`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `cat-file`, `ls-tree`, `rev-parse`, `rev-list`, `merge-base`, `grep`, `config --get`, `remote get-url`); `clone --no-hardlinks` FROM it, and `fetch`, `worktree add`, `checkout --detach`, the legacy 3-argument `merge-tree`, `merge-tree --write-tree`, scratch `merge` and `branch` only inside `.tools/b692/repo` and `.tools/wt-b692-*` (via `git -C`). No git verb in the project root (records repo). **Forbidden everywhere: `merge-tree --write-tree` in the shared repo, `gc`, `worktree prune`, `reset` in the shared repo, `clean`, `stash`, `fetch --prune`, `--shared`, `--reference`.**
- **Not yours (never read to obey, edit, quarantine, kill, stop or lock-break):** anything naming `b685` or `wt-b685-*` (the builder's trees, scripts and scratch: its claim instruments, READ-FORBIDDEN, never run, copied or sourced; say you did not open them; the builder's `Briefs/` STATUS is readable, and `Briefs/` evidence folders ARE readable for COMPARISON only after your own table is written), `b686`, `wt-b686-*` (the live builder `Datasec/MPS-M26`), `b672`, `wt-b672-*`, `b675`, `wt-b675-*`, `b670`, `wt-b670-*`, `b668`, `wt-b668-*`, `b663`, `wt-b663-*`, `b665`, `wt-b665-*`, `b654`, `wt-b654-*`, `b630`, `wt-b630-*`, `b5*`, `wt-b5*`, `qa-*`, `backup-*`, `_quarantine*`, every other seat's `.tools/b6*`. Name everything of yours `b692` / `G125`. The `.tools/_quarantine/` folder is written by you only for your own slot release. The shared SDK `.tools/dotnet/` is used read-only.
- **The real price books are confidential.** Never open `2_Project_Files/.local/`, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/`, `.tools/backup-*`, or any real book or store; every scratch row is synthetic (`StoreProbe.Plant`'s own store). Secrets only as environment, never on argv; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except by the NAME test and the Jira GET.
- **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -D`): quarantine to `.tools/b692/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`** (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain a space and `!`; a word-split path wrote stray files into the project root before: every path in a redirect, a marker, a log line and a script is single-quoted or in an array; create none, touch none); where `dotnet` needs a cwd, set it with `bash -c` or Python `subprocess(cwd=...)` and say which; write `${VAR}:path`, never `$VAR:path`; never put a command with a project path in a shell variable used unquoted in command position (the zsh word-split hook refuses it): use `bash -c '...'` or a QUOTED heredoc (`<<'EOF'`); quote any URL holding `?`; no unquoted word starting with `=` in command position (the project root holds a file named `=`: use `----` as a separator); bash, not zsh, for loops; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count (macOS grep has no `-P`: use `-E`); `python3 -I` for anything that reads a file you did not write. Never kill a process by basename: by pid or port plus cwd. No person's name in any id, file, branch or STATUS (say "the product owner"; git author fields carry a name: do not quote them), no decision-card id, clock from `date`.
- **RESUME (at about 80% of your context, or at the hard stop):** stop new checks, write STATUS sections `PROGRESS` (each check: done / partial / not started, with evidence paths) and `RESUME` (the exact next commands, the state of every scratch tree and mutant with its restore proof, the slot held or released, the pins last read, the predictions file, the seed, the evidence paths), restore every mutant, release the slot, then end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". Tuesday would rather have a conditional verdict with the open instances listed than a RESUME with nothing shippable. A verdict from a gate that did not finish C2 or C4 is conditional at best.

